From 95bc82b3fb1f8aaba7d637cdb4c6fb3b9b9cd857 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thiago Duarte <me@tduarte.co>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:12:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] media: qcom: camss: csid-340: Widen the PHY select field
 to three bits

CSID_CSI2_RX_CFG0 selects the input PHY as csiphy index + 1 in a field
defined as GENMASK(21, 20). With four CSIPHYs, as on Milos, the fourth one
needs the value 4, which does not fit: the field is written as 0 and the
CSID listens to no PHY. A sensor on csiphy3 then streams (its frame counter
runs) while the capture never completes a frame.

The downstream TFE CSID drivers use a three bit mask for this field
(csi2_rx_phy_num_mask = 0x7 in cam_tfe_csid530.h and cam_tfe_csid640.h),
and bit 22 is not otherwise used here. Use GENMASK(22, 20).

Tested on a Fairphone (Gen. 6): the front sensor on csiphy3 delivers
frames with this change and none without it; csiphy1 keeps working.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
index 9a5a6710c0c6..689a76935b1f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csid-340.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 #define CSID_CSI2_RX_CFG0					(0x100)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_NUM_ACTIVE_LANES_MASK	GENMASK(1, 0)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_DLX_INPUT_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(17, 4)
-#define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(21, 20)
+#define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_MASK		GENMASK(22, 20)
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_NUM_SEL_BASE_IDX	1
 #define		CSI2_RX_CFG0_PHY_TYPE_SEL		BIT(24)
 
